WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.050
- We are back

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.400
and I can never say enough

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.620
about how grateful I am for my fans.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.550
Y'all have inspired me.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.900
They've been with me for like, 20 years.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.070
Thank you so much.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.010
I love meeting my fans, it's
the coolest experience ever,

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.480
especially to connect through music.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.530
It's the coolest thing ever.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.937
Most celebrities do.

00:00:14.937 --> 00:00:16.230
But every once in a while,

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.240
we have an encounter so over the top,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.490
it stays in our minds forever,

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.870
'cause you're like, "That happened."

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.060
And mine happened in a
bathroom of all places,

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.890
and I've interviewed many people

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.020
whose encounters were even more unusual,

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.370
which I was like, "Really?"

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.750
So, just take a look.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.610
- I was in a commercial center,

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.380
I went to the toilet

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.300
and, yeah.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.580
And then I was about to wee,

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.056
and then I just feel...

00:00:40.056 --> 00:00:40.889
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:00:40.889 --> 00:00:42.000
I just feel someone staring at me

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.980
and I'm like.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.660
And this guy, very happy,

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.717
and he just says,

00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:48.631
"Are you the smiley guy from Ted Lasso?"

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:49.500
(everybody laughing)

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.850
Not even my character.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.754
And I'm like, "Um, yeah?"

00:00:52.754 --> 00:00:54.063
And he just goes like,

00:00:54.937 --> 00:00:56.252
"Can I have picture?"

00:00:56.252 --> 00:00:57.492
(everyone laughing)

00:00:57.492 --> 00:00:58.980
- Can you give me a minute?

00:00:58.980 --> 00:00:59.813
- Not right now.

00:00:59.813 --> 00:01:01.470
- And I was like, "Um okay."

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.500
- You're like, shaking.
(laughing hysterically)

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.660
- Bathrooms are just

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:07.530
- [Kelly] You get trapped.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.363
- You get trapped. Yeah.

00:01:08.363 --> 00:01:10.200
And it's the worst for me,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.560
'cause it's like, teenage
girls just follow me in

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.030
and it'll be like, a squad.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:15.960
You know, if I go to Disneyland,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.330
there's like, squads of
teenage girls that'll go

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:19.680
and they'll follow me in a bathroom

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.513
and then you come out

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.910
and you're bombarded
with seven random girls

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:24.780
just waiting there

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.212
and you're like, "Hello. Thank you."

00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:29.077
- I please hope that you go,

00:01:29.077 --> 00:01:30.633
"It all went well, thank you."

00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:31.466
(everybody laughing)

00:01:31.466 --> 00:01:32.820
And just keep walking. (laughing)

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.150
I know you had to have
had crazy passionate fans.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:36.983
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:40.230
There's a list of just
crazy memories and--

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.063
- [Kelly] I can't imagine.

00:01:41.063 --> 00:01:44.310
- --fan experiences from being in Brazil

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.450
and having thousands of
fans break into our hotel

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.283
and they had to call

00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:51.420
the Brazilian National
Guard to get them out.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.253
- What?

00:01:52.253 --> 00:01:53.460
- These are very passionate fans.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.460
I mean, it's why the books
and movies are so successful

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.950
is these fans, they don't give up.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:01:59.850
They get what they want.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.860
- I love the books and movies.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.230
I would never break into your hotel room.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.404
There are normal fans.

00:02:05.404 --> 00:02:07.050
(both laughing)

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.793
There are people who
just appreciate the art.

00:02:08.793 --> 00:02:09.960
(audience laughing)

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:10.793
- There was a time,

00:02:10.793 --> 00:02:12.330
I think we were in Santiago, Chile,

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.040
and our fans were going crazy

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.750
and we got into the airport.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:16.746
- What?

00:02:16.746 --> 00:02:17.579
- They finally got us to the bus.

00:02:17.579 --> 00:02:19.710
We have to walk through people,
over people, under people.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:20.543
It was crazy,

00:02:20.543 --> 00:02:21.390
but as we were driving away,

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:22.950
there was continuous banging,

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.900
and we were literally
miles from the airport,

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.560
and there were fans on top of
the bus banging on the bus.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.231
We saw hands coming through the skylight

00:02:30.231 --> 00:02:31.785
(everyone laughing)

00:02:31.785 --> 00:02:33.163
and yeah.

00:02:33.163 --> 00:02:33.996
The levels of love.

00:02:33.996 --> 00:02:35.820
- Okay, I really like Meryl Streep

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.590
but I'm never gonna
climb on her car and...

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.930
(everyone laughing)

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:40.763
Everyone loves you.

00:02:40.763 --> 00:02:42.210
You've done so many things

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.220
but do people like, out
of all your stuff, though,

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.540
do people, when you're
in a hardware store,

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.392
do they still do the (Tim Allen grunt)?

00:02:47.392 --> 00:02:48.225
(Tim Allen grunting)

00:02:48.225 --> 00:02:49.058
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:49.058 --> 00:02:50.253
- It's "Grunt for me."

00:02:50.253 --> 00:02:51.432
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:51.432 --> 00:02:52.860
You know, like I'm one
of those little monkeys

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.967
that does this, you know?

00:02:53.967 --> 00:02:55.170
- [Kelly] But they ask you?

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.870
- If they come and "Grunt
for me. Show the kids."

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.670
Or a cop pulls me over

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:02.130
'cause I have a very high-performance car

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:03.180
and it was making too much noise.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.962
As soon as the window goes
down, he goes (grunting)

00:03:05.962 --> 00:03:06.795
(everyone laughing)

00:03:06.795 --> 00:03:07.710
(Kelly clapping)

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.472
I'm not gonna get...

00:03:09.472 --> 00:03:11.400
- Hey, if it gets you out of the ticket,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.530
I'd (grunting) all day long.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:14.679
- It actually didn't.

00:03:14.679 --> 00:03:16.440
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.970
- This is a true story.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:18.960
This is about two years ago.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:19.860
I was walking to work,

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.517
some girl stop me and was like,

00:03:21.517 --> 00:03:22.710
"Hey, I just want to let you know,

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:26.250
you got me through a lot
of tough times in my life.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.340
But watching your sketches
and watching your jokes,

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.173
it just got me through."

00:03:30.173 --> 00:03:32.340
I go "Oh, appreciate it. That's awesome."

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.300
So I go, "I'm happy you're here."

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.130
And we talked for about 20 minutes,

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.617
and then she goes, "Can I have a picture?"

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.300
And I go "Yeah, of course."

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.900
So we took a picture, and we pose.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.067
"Can I have one for Snapchat?"

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:46.170
And I go, "Yeah, of course."

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.058
So we take one for Snapchat.

00:03:48.058 --> 00:03:48.891
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:03:48.891 --> 00:03:50.443
And she goes, "Okay, well,
I'll talk to you later."

00:03:50.443 --> 00:03:51.510
I go, "Hey, nice to meet you,"

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:52.650
She's walking away,

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.850
and as she's walking away, I swear,

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.748
she goes, "Oh my gosh, I can't
believe I met Jimmy Kimmel."

00:03:56.748 --> 00:03:59.748
(everyone laughing)

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.616
20 minutes I was talking to this person.

00:04:04.616 --> 00:04:07.407
- (laughing) That's so amazing.

